"As the beelogger.csv file becomes too large, you may discard or archive former data. To do so, enter your split data in the bottom line: Archive name: if you leave the field unchanged, a file called Archive 'start date'-'end date'.csv will be created Example: 'Archive250418-050918.csv' You can of course enter any name (e.g.: 'beeloggerdaten2017') (.csv is added automatically).<br>Then select the start date and end date for the archive file. For the remaining beelogger.csv you need to choose a start date, while the end date is defined by the most recent record date.<br>The file splitting is enabled in the selection field: <split files></span>, which must then be confirmed by 'yes'. <br>The action is effective only after saving the Configuration page (at the very bottom of the page)!<br>Data download is managed directly below the archive function.<br>To delete a csv-file (except beelogger.csv, month.csv and week.csv), just select the file from the right field. When saving the Configuration, the file will be deleted",
"Remote control is available for all WLAN, GSM and LTE beeloggers which have a server connection. The measurement and transmission intervals, their regular changeover and the measurement of the signal strength can be set. This ensures that relevant time periods are logged more closely than less relevant ones thus saving data volume.<br>For beeloggers without EE-PROM, the transmission interval equals the measurement interval.<br> Ideally, WLAN, GSM or LTE should comprise an EE-PROM to keep the amount of data at minimum and avoid transmission losses.<br>The measurement and transmission intervals can be managed by the microcontroller or by the server.<br><br>All modes distinguish between daytime / nighttime and summer / winter periods and schedules.<br>The winter period can be disabled and the beelogger will work according to the summer schedules.<br><br>The operating modes are as follows:<br><br>- Sketch-controlled mode: The beelogger uses the values and schedules which were directly programmed in the beelogger sketch. No difference is made between summer and winter periods.<br><br>- Time-controlled mode: The measurment and transmission intervals are managed under the Configuration page of the server. Changes can be made at any time, but apply beginning after the next transmission <br><br>- Light-controlled mode: The light-controlled mode requires the beelogger to be equipped with the luminosity sensor: BH1750FVI. As soon as the sensor detects a first daylight, the system switches to the summer daytime interval - when the value drops below 1, the beelogger switches to the summer nighttime interval. In winter, the beelogger runs throughout with the winter interval (or the summer intervals if winter interval = 'disabled') - independently of the luminosity sensor. <br><br>- Solar voltage-controlled mode (only for beelogger with solarcell): As soon as the solarcell detects the daylight, it switches to the summer daytime interval - if the value drops to 0.3, the beelogger changes over to the summer nighttime interval. In winter, the beelogger runs with the winter interval (or the summer intervals if winter interval = 'disabled') - independent of the solar module.<br><br>Transmission cycle (only for EE-PROM beeloggers): Here you can set the transmission cycle for EE-PROM beeloggers.<br><br>Service parameter: All values captured by the beelogger are only transmitted to the server during the next transmission and appear under the data set 'Service'<br>",
