"This function adds automatically notes when changes occur on or around the hive.<br>If the automatic notes are 'enabled', a label “G?” and  a note are added as soon as a weight loss is detected that exceeds the weight threshold. Depending on the threshold, for each event such as a honey top box set up, inspection, harvest etc., the note comprising the abbreviation 'G?' and the description: 'Weight loss of ... kg detected'. The detected weight loss is directly shown in kg. You can then simply edit or delete the automatic note. In winter, the measured kg value could for instance directly represent the added feed weight. The next automatic note can be generated at the earliest after the dead-time specified in the respective field. A value of 20 minutes has proven to be useful in practice in order to avoid two automatic notes (lid / frame / box removed or added) referring to the same inspection, for example.<br>If you enable the D2 service switch before the inspection and then disable it afterwards, the inspection icon is automatically added",
"The beelogger sketch triggers a special routine as soon as a weight loss of more than 1kg (standard settings) is detected. The following next measurements will be directly sent to the server.<br><br>If the swarm alarm is enabled, the server checks whether a weight loss exceeding the threshold set in the Configuration, has occurred. Hence, all transmitted values are checked. If the loss persists, the server sends out an alert message by e-mail or Telegram-/Pushover mail as set up in the Configuration.<br>This procedure has the advantage that all beekeeping activities, such as: 'Removing the honey frame for inspection and reinstalling it after 20 minutes', do not trigger a swarm alarm - provided that the 'reference time' is choosen longer than normal inspection times. <br>In addition, each swarm alarm automatically generates a note related to the data set 'weight'.<br> In case of possible successive swarms, each swarm gets its own index and the last swarm alert message is displayed on the beeloggerShow page. All swarms messages can be reviewed with their time of occurrance under the Notes section.<br>You can also delete the swarm message. Check the 'Yes' box and save the Configuration.<br>Swarm alarm by e-mail: Please note that the web server must be able to send out emails (community members can do this automatically)!<br><br>Swarm alarm by Pushover mail: To be able to use Pushover messaging the user must install the Pushover app on his mobile device and create a user account. The use of the service may incur costs (approx. 5€ once - as of August 2018). After 'Pushover' account creation you will receive a user name and a token for the use of the application. The credentials must be entered here.<br><br>Telegram: create Token(Bot-Token) and Chat-ID, using the Telegram Messenger<br><br>To use the e-mail or Telegram-/Pushover mail swarm alarms, they must be enabled and set up on the Configuration page.<br>Reference time means the period of time whilst the server checks the weight loss.<br>The weight in grams or kg indicates the minimum loss amount between the reference weight and the current weight required to trigger a swarm alarm.<br>Finally, the sender and the recipient of the email must be set up. It is important to note that on many (mail) servers email addresses out of domain may be prohibited by information security rules and be considered as spam or rejected.",
